  "content": {
    "id": "p37-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "Among twenty-nine games of football played by eight teams, prove that there is some pair of teams who play each other more than once.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Some pair of teams plays at least twice.\n\nThere are only $\\binom{8}{2}=28$ pairs of teams, so the pigeonhole principle applies to the 29 games.",
      "worked": "There are $\\binom{8}{2}=28$ possible pairs of teams. Label 28 holes with these pairs and place each of the 29 games into the hole corresponding to its two teams. By the pigeonhole principle, some hole contains at least two games. Therefore, some pair of teams plays each other more than once.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
